---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { SITE, PRICE } from "../consts";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../lib/schema";

const crumbs = [
	{ label: "Home", href: "/" },
	{ label: "About", href: "/about/" },
];
---

<Page
	title="About"
	heading="Why this exists"
	description={`${SITE.name} is made by ${SITE.company}, a small software company in the ${SITE.companyCountry}. One-time pricing, local processing, no data collection.`}
	intro="Soft Clipper started as a tool for one person with a backlog of long recordings and no time to cut them. It got sold because everyone who saw it asked for a copy."
	eyebrow="About"
	crumbs={crumbs}
	schema={[breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)]}
	narrow
>
	<section class="pt-0">
		<div class="wrap wrap-narrow prose">
			<h2>What we decided early</h2>
			<p>
				Three decisions shaped the product, and all three cost us money on paper.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>It runs on your computer.</strong> Uploading a two-hour recording to a server
				and waiting is slower than encoding it locally, and it means someone else holds your
				footage. Local processing also removes the reason to meter you by the minute.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>You pay once.</strong> Recurring revenue is better for us and worse for you on
				a tool you might use twice a month. {PRICE.display} once, and the app keeps working
				whether or not we ever hear from you again.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>You bring your own AI key.</strong> AI analysis has a real per-video cost. We
				could bury it in a subscription; instead the app uses your own Google Gemini key, which
				is free for ordinary use. It means one extra setup step and no ongoing bill.
			</p>

			<h2>What we are not</h2>
			<p>
				Not a cloud platform, not a scheduler, not a social media manager and not a video
				editor. Soft Clipper does one job: long video in, postable vertical clips out. Anything
				it does not do is listed openly on the <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> rather than
				discovered after purchase.
			</p>

			<h2>The company</h2>
			<p>
				{SITE.name} is published by {SITE.company}, registered in the {SITE.companyCountry}.
				Support goes to a person, not a ticket queue:
				<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Where it is going</h2>
			<p>
				A browser version is in development for people who are not on Windows. It will be sold
				separately and will not change anything about the desktop licence you own.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Page>

<style>
	.pt-0 {
		padding-top: 8px;
	}
</style>
